Day 14
-------

INHERITANCE:
-----------
Acquiring all the properties(variables) and behaviour(methods) from one class to another class is called inheritance.


Objective
.........
1)re-usability
2)Avoid duplication

types
-----
1)single -> 1 parent and 1 child
2)multi level ->1 parent child grandchild 
3)hierarchy ->1 parent multiple child
4)multiple ->multiple parents single child, it is implement using interfaces,      not class

NOTE:Why Doesn't Java Support Multiple Inheritance?

The main reason is to avoid the Diamond Problem.-or-Java cannot decide automatically. This ambiguity is called the Diamond Problem.
To avoid this confusion, Java does not support multiple inheritance with classes.

extends keyword not support 2 class at a time it will cause ambiguity bcs of duplicate method




Interview Questions
1. Does Java support multiple inheritance?
With classes: ❌ No
With interfaces: ✅ Yes
2. Why doesn't Java support multiple inheritance with classes?

To avoid ambiguity caused by the Diamond Problem.

3. How is multiple inheritance achieved in Java?

By implementing multiple interfaces using the implements keyword.

4. Can a class extend multiple classes?

No. A class can extend only one class.

5. Can a class implement multiple interfaces?

Yes.

interface A { }
interface B { }

class C implements A, B {

}
